.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1019 AM PST Thu Nov 12 2026

Today is a transition day as a cold front gradually approaches.
We will see high clouds roll in through the day, then lower this
evening into tonight as southerly winds gradually strengthen. Rain
chances (up to 20%) kick in after midnight, then increase and
solidify midmorning with accompanying winds as the front moves
in.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR through the rest of today. Southerly winds
gradually increase through the forecast period, potentially reaching
20-25kt ahead of the front. High confidence in occurrence, but
medium confidence in exact timing of a ceiling forming tonight and
then lowering into MVFR territory around midnight as the low
pressure system nears. Up to 20% chance for rain at SFO as early
as 11z, but confidence in rain is too low to add in RA or VCSH
until 17z.

SFO Bridge Approach...The approach from SJC to SFO is currently
clear and should stay that way during the day today. A high ceiling
should form late tonight and is expected with moderate confidence to
lower below 5000ft around midnight.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR conditions are expected to prevail
through the forecast period as a developing cold front begins to
push through our area to the north, eventually reaching the
Monterey Bay terminal just outside the end of the forecast period.

