.MARINE...
(Today through Tuesday)
Issued at 1019 AM PST Thu Nov 12 2026

Fresh to strong southerly winds will increase to near gale force
overnight into Friday morning as a cold front pushes through our
area. After the front passes winds will shift to westerly and
decrease to a moderate breeze by Friday afternoon. Meanwhile WNW
swell from a distant hurricane force low will build to very high
with significant wave heights up to 25 feet by Saturday morning.
Wave heights decrease slightly Sunday before another round of high
seas moves into the coastal waters on Monday. Small crafts will
sustain heavy damage and may not survive in these extreme sea
states.

